{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WrzMS8xt15NypvZUcc16k6","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended\n     2→title: \"List directory contents via ls (extended flags)\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go ls binary with extended flags (-C, -x, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i,\n     6→  -s, -n, -F, -R) on a fixture directory. The differential testing harness runs both the Go\n     7→  binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gls from coreutils) with the same arguments and\n     8→  environment, applies an LsExtendedNormalizer (which extends the core LsNormalizer with\n     9→  mtime replacement across recursive subdirectory listings), and confirms that the normalized\n    10→  outputs are identical. All tests use LC_ALL=C and --color=never. Fixture files have\n    11→  controlled sizes, mtimes, and permissions to ensure deterministic sort order.\n    12→\n    13→actor: Human Operator\n    14→\n    15→trigger: |\n    16→  The operator has completed prd010-ls-extended.yaml (extended flags PRD) and the core\n    17→  ls PRD (prd008-ls.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce a passing differential test for\n    18→  cmd/ls extended flags.\n    19→\n    20→flow:\n    21→  - id: F1\n    22→    step: |\n    23→      The operator runs the Go ls binary with extended flags on a fixture directory with\n    24→      controlled file sizes, mtimes, and types. Example: ./bin/ls -lR --color=never testdata/ls-fixture/\n    25→  - id: F2\n    26→    step: |\n    27→      cmd/ls reads directory entries and obtains file metadata via pkg/sys.Stat for sort-by-time\n    28→      (-t), sort-by-size (-S), inode display (-i), and block count display (-s). It formats\n    29→      multi-column output via pkg/format.Columns for -C and -x modes.\n    30→  - id: F3\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      For -R (recursive), cmd/ls descends into each subdirectory and prints a \"path:\" header\n    33→      followed by the directory contents in the active format mode. Each subdirectory listing\n    34→      applies the same flags (sort, filter, format, metadata).\n    35→  - id: F4\n    36→    step: |\n    37→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/ls and gls with\n    38→      the same arguments, environment (LC_ALL=C, --color=never), and working directory.\n    39→  - id: F5\n    40→    step: |\n    41→      The harness applies the LsExtendedNormalizer to both outputs. This normalizer replaces\n    42→      all mtime fields (in long-format output and in recursive subdirectory listings) with the\n    43→      placeholder \"MTIME\". Inode numbers and block counts are not normalized; both binaries\n    44→      stat the same files on the same filesystem, producing identical values.\n    45→  - id: F6\n    46→    step: |\n    47→      The harness compares the normalized outputs byte-for-byte. Both binaries must produce\n    48→      identical sort order, column layout, metadata values, type indicators, and recursive\n    49→      subdirectory structure.\n    50→  - id: F7\n    51→    step: |\n    52→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    53→      triggering args, both raw outputs, both normalized outputs, and both exit codes.\n    54→\n    55→touchpoints:\n    56→  - T1: \"cmd/ls — multi-column layout, sort order, metadata display, classify, recursive (prd010-ls-extended R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6)\"\n    57→  - T2: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, Stat/Lstat for mtime, size, inode, blocks\"\n    58→  - T3: \"pkg/format — Columns for -C/-x, FileTypeColor, HumanSize for -s -h\"\n    59→  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, LsExtendedNormalizer\"\n    60→\n    61→success_criteria:\n    62→  - id: S1\n    63→    criterion: |\n    64→      -C produces multi-column output even when stdout is piped, matching gls -C output on\n    65→      the same fixture with a fixed column width.\n    66→  - id: S2\n    67→    criterion: |\n    68→      -x produces horizontal-sorted multi-column output, matching gls -x.\n    69→  - id: S3\n    70→    criterion: |\n    71→      -t sorts entries by modification time (newest first) on a fixture with files of known\n    72→      distinct mtimes, matching gls -t output.\n    73→  - id: S4\n    74→    criterion: |\n    75→      -S sorts entries by size (largest first), matching gls -S output.\n    76→  - id: S5\n    77→    criterion: |\n    78→      -r reverses the sort order, matching gls -r output.\n    79→  - id: S6\n    80→    criterion: |\n    81→      -i prepends inode numbers to each entry, matching gls -i on the same fixture.\n    82→  - id: S7\n    83→    criterion: |\n    84→      -s prepends block counts to each entry, matching gls -s on the same fixture.\n    85→  - id: S8\n    86→    criterion: |\n    87→      -n produces long format with numeric UID/GID instead of names, matching gls -n after\n    88→      MTIME normalization.\n    89→  - id: S9\n    90→    criterion: |\n    91→      -F appends type indicators (/, *, @, |, =) matching gls -F on a fixture with a\n    92→      directory, executable, symlink, and named pipe.\n    93→  - id: S10\n    94→    criterion: |\n    95→      -R recursively lists subdirectories with \"path:\" headers and blank-line separators,\n    96→      matching gls -R after MTIME normalization.\n    97→  - id: S11\n    98→    criterion: |\n    99→      The differential test passes for all extended flags: -C, -x, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i,\n   100→      -s, -n, -F, -R, and combinations (-Rl, -tr, -SF).\n   101→\n   102→out_of_scope:\n   103→  - -v (version sort) test uses a simple fixture with files named file1, file2, file10;\n   104→    full strverscmp edge cases are not exercised in the differential test.\n   105→  - -U (unsorted) output order depends on filesystem directory order; both binaries produce\n   106→    the same order when reading the same directory, so comparison is valid but not a test\n   107→    of Go-specific behavior.\n   108→  - SIGWINCH and terminal resize behavior during -R recursive listing is not testable in the\n   109→    differential harness.\n   110→\n   111→test_suite: test-rel04.1\n   112→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ab6c3f3-6c03-4d5b-9d8b-ea4468f3b690","uuid":"b20fd6cb-e44d-4d56-bd55-816c08d7c040","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/310/docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended.yaml","content":"id: rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended\ntitle: \"List directory contents via ls (extended flags)\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go ls binary with extended flags (-C, -x, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i,\n  -s, -n, -F, -R) on a fixture directory. The differential testing harness runs both the Go\n  binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gls from coreutils) with the same arguments and\n  environment, applies an LsExtendedNormalizer (which extends the core LsNormalizer with\n  mtime replacement across recursive subdirectory listings), and confirms that the normalized\n  outputs are identical. All tests use LC_ALL=C and --color=never. Fixture files have\n  controlled sizes, mtimes, and permissions to ensure deterministic sort order.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed prd010-ls-extended.yaml (extended flags PRD) and the core\n  ls PRD (prd008-ls.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce a passing differential test for\n  cmd/ls extended flags.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go ls binary with extended flags on a fixture directory with\n      controlled file sizes, mtimes, and types. Example: ./bin/ls -lR --color=never testdata/ls-fixture/\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/ls reads directory entries and obtains file metadata via pkg/sys.Stat for sort-by-time\n      (-t), sort-by-size (-S), inode display (-i), and block count display (-s). It formats\n      multi-column output via pkg/format.Columns for -C and -x modes.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      For -R (recursive), cmd/ls descends into each subdirectory and prints a \"path:\" header\n      followed by the directory contents in the active format mode. Each subdirectory listing\n      applies the same flags (sort, filter, format, metadata).\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/ls and gls with\n      the same arguments, environment (LC_ALL=C, --color=never), and working directory.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness applies the LsExtendedNormalizer to both outputs. This normalizer replaces\n      all mtime fields (in long-format output and in recursive subdirectory listings) with the\n      placeholder \"MTIME\". Inode numbers and block counts are not normalized; both binaries\n      stat the same files on the same filesystem, producing identical values.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The harness compares the normalized outputs byte-for-byte. Both binaries must produce\n      identical sort order, column layout, metadata values, type indicators, and recursive\n      subdirectory structure.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both raw outputs, both normalized outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/ls — multi-column layout, sort order, metadata display, classify, recursive (prd010-ls-extended R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, Stat/Lstat for mtime, size, inode, blocks\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/format — Columns for -C/-x, FileTypeColor, HumanSize for -s -h\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, LsExtendedNormalizer\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: |\n      -C produces multi-column output even when stdout is piped, matching gls -C output on\n      the same fixture with a fixed column width.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      -x produces horizontal-sorted multi-column output, matching gls -x.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      -t sorts entries by modification time (newest first) on a fixture with files of known\n      distinct mtimes, matching gls -t output.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      -S sorts entries by size (largest first), matching gls -S output.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      -r reverses the sort order, matching gls -r output.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      -i prepends inode numbers to each entry, matching gls -i on the same fixture.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      -s prepends block counts to each entry, matching gls -s on the same fixture.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: |\n      -n produces long format with numeric UID/GID instead of names, matching gls -n after\n      MTIME normalization.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: |\n      -F appends type indicators (/, *, @, |, =) matching gls -F on a fixture with a\n      directory, executable, symlink, and named pipe.\n  - id: S10\n    criterion: |\n      -R recursively lists subdirectories with \"path:\" headers and blank-line separators,\n      matching gls -R after MTIME normalization.\n  - id: S11\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for all extended flags: -C, -x, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i,\n      -s, -n, -F, -R, and combinations (-Rl, -tr, -SF).\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - -v (version sort) test uses a simple fixture with files named file1, file2, file10;\n    full strverscmp edge cases are not exercised in the differential test.\n  - -U (unsorted) output order depends on filesystem directory order; both binaries produce\n    the same order when reading the same directory, so comparison is valid but not a test\n    of Go-specific behavior.\n  - SIGWINCH and terminal resize behavior during -R recursive listing is not testable in the\n    differential harness.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel04.1\n","numLines":112,"startLine":1,"totalLines":112}}}
