{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q46ufWxC8CupRr1iy3PHog","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel04.1\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel04.1 — ls extended flag listing\"\n     3→release: rel04.1\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended\n     7→  - prd010-ls-extended R1\n     8→  - prd010-ls-extended R2\n     9→  - prd010-ls-extended R3\n    10→  - prd010-ls-extended R4\n    11→  - prd010-ls-extended R5\n    12→  - prd010-ls-extended R6\n    13→\n    14→preconditions:\n    15→  - ./bin/ls exists (built via mage build).\n    16→  - The reference binary gls is installed (brew install coreutils) and on PATH.\n    17→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/ls/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    18→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C and --color=never to eliminate locale and ANSI variance.\n    19→  - The LsExtendedNormalizer replaces mtime columns with MTIME in all output including recursive subdirectory listings.\n    20→  - Both binaries run on the same fixture directory on the same filesystem, ensuring inode numbers and block counts are identical.\n    21→  - \"Fixture directory (testdata/ls-extended-fixture/) contains files with distinct known sizes, files with distinct mtimes set via os.Chtimes, subdirectories with nested files for -R testing, a symbolic link, an executable file (mode 0755), a named pipe (FIFO), files named file1/file2/file10/file20 for -v version sort testing, and dotfiles for filter interaction with -R.\"\n    22→\n    23→test_cases:\n    24→  # --- uc001-ls-extended: ls extended flag listing ---\n    25→\n    26→  - name: multi_col_forced\n    27→    description: -C forces multi-column output even when stdout is piped. stdout is a pipe; -C overrides single-column default\n    28→    inputs:\n    29→      args: [\"-C\", \"--color=never\", \"-w\", \"80\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n    30→      stdin: null\n    31→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    32→    normalization: none\n    33→    expected:\n    34→      exit_code: 0\n    35→      stdout_structure: entries in columns, fitting within 80 characters\n    36→      stderr: \"\"\n    37→    traces:\n    38→      - prd010-ls-extended R1.1\n    39→      - prd010-ls-extended R1.2\n    40→\n    41→  - name: horizontal_layout\n    42→    description: -x sorts entries horizontally (across, then down).\n    43→    inputs:\n    44→      args: [\"-x\", \"--color=never\", \"-w\", \"80\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n    45→      stdin: null\n    46→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    47→    normalization: none\n    48→    expected:\n    49→      exit_code: 0\n    50→      stdout_structure: entries arranged across rows first, then down\n    51→      stderr: \"\"\n    52→    traces:\n    53→      - prd010-ls-extended R1.3\n    54→\n    55→  - name: sort_by_mtime\n    56→    description: '-t sorts by modification time, newest first. Fixture files have distinct mtimes set via os.Chtimes: newest_file (mtime = now), middle_file (mtime = now - 1h), oldest_file (mtime = now - 2h)'\n    57→    inputs:\n    58→      args: [\"-1t\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n    59→      stdin: null\n    60→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    61→    normalization: none\n    62→    expected:\n    63→      exit_code: 0\n    64→      stdout_structure: entries ordered newest to oldest\n    65→      stderr: \"\"\n    66→    traces:\n    67→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.1\n    68→\n    69→  - name: sort_by_size\n    70→    description: -S sorts by size, largest first.\n    71→    inputs:\n    72→      args: [\"-1S\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n    73→      stdin: null\n    74→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    75→    normalization: none\n    76→    expected:\n    77→      exit_code: 0\n    78→      stdout_structure: entries ordered largest to smallest by file size\n    79→      stderr: \"\"\n    80→    traces:\n    81→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.2\n    82→\n    83→  - name: sort_reverse\n    84→    description: -r reverses the default alphabetical sort order.\n    85→    inputs:\n    86→      args: [\"-1r\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n    87→      stdin: null\n    88→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    89→    normalization: none\n    90→    expected:\n    91→      exit_code: 0\n    92→      stdout_structure: entries in reverse C locale alphabetical order\n    93→      stderr: \"\"\n    94→    traces:\n    95→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.3\n    96→\n    97→  - name: sort_reverse_time\n    98→    description: -tr reverses time sort (oldest first).\n    99→    inputs:\n   100→      args: [\"-1tr\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   101→      stdin: null\n   102→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   103→    normalization: none\n   104→    expected:\n   105→      exit_code: 0\n   106→      stdout_structure: entries ordered oldest to newest\n   107→      stderr: \"\"\n   108→    traces:\n   109→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.3\n   110→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.1\n   111→\n   112→  - name: sort_unsorted\n   113→    description: -U disables sorting; entries in directory order.\n   114→    inputs:\n   115→      args: [\"-1U\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   116→      stdin: null\n   117→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   118→    normalization: none\n   119→    expected:\n   120→      exit_code: 0\n   121→      stdout_structure: entries in directory order (same for both binaries on same filesystem)\n   122→      stderr: \"\"\n   123→    traces:\n   124→      - prd010-ls-extended R2.4\n   125→\n   126→  - name: version_sort\n   127→    description: -v sorts with numeric-aware version sort (file2 before file10).\n   128→    inputs:\n   129→      args: [\"-1v\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   130→      stdin: null\n   131→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   132→    normalization: none\n   133→    expected:\n   134→      exit_code: 0\n   135→      stdout_str