executable (gets *), a symlink (gets @), a named pipe (gets |), a regular file (no indicator).'\n   185→    inputs:\n   186→      args: [\"-1F\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   187→      stdin: null\n   188→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   189→    normalization: none\n   190→    expected:\n   191→      exit_code: 0\n   192→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"/\", \"*\", and \"@\"'\n   193→      stderr: \"\"\n   194→    traces:\n   195→      - prd010-ls-extended R4.1\n   196→      - prd010-ls-extended R4.2\n   197→\n   198→  - name: recursive\n   199→    description: -R recursively lists subdirectories with \"path:\" headers.\n   200→    inputs:\n   201→      args: [\"-1R\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   202→      stdin: null\n   203→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   204→    normalization: none\n   205→    expected:\n   206→      exit_code: 0\n   207→      stdout_structure: |\n   208→        Root listing followed by subdirectory listings, each with \"path:\" header\n   209→        and blank-line separators.\n   210→      stderr: \"\"\n   211→    traces:\n   212→      - prd010-ls-extended R5.1\n   213→      - prd010-ls-extended R5.3\n   214→      - prd010-ls-extended R5.4\n   215→\n   216→  - name: recursive_long\n   217→    description: -Rl lists all subdirectories in long format with \"total N\" per directory.\n   218→    inputs:\n   219→      args: [\"-Rl\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-extended-fixture/\"]\n   220→      stdin: null\n   221→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   222→    normalization: LsExtendedNormalizer replaces all mtime columns with MTIME\n   223→    expected:\n   224→      exit_code: 0\n   225→      stdout_structure: |\n   226→        Each subdirectory block has \"path:\" header, \"total N\" line, and long-format entries\n   227→        with MTIME placeholder.\n   228→      stderr: \"\"\n   229→    traces:\n   230→      - prd010-ls-extended R5.2\n   231→      - prd010-ls-extended R6.3\n   232→"